  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain showers are expected tomorrow into Monday,\nwith best chances across Central NY as a slow moving Nor'easter\ngrazes the area.\n\n\nAn unseasonably strong coastal low off the Delmarva will remain\nin place today while maturing and occluding. The coastal low \nwill then complete a cyclonic loop to the south of Long Island \ntonight through Sunday, nearing the Jersey shore by late Sunday \nand Sunday night. The westward drift in the position of the \nvertically stacked low will advect Atlantic moisture westward \nacross NY/PA, with thickening and lowering clouds. The first \nchance of showers will reach central NY Sunday morning, then \nprogress gradually westward as an inverted trough axis north of \nthe low center rotates westward. Showers may reach the Genesee \nValley and western Finger Lakes by early to mid afternoon. Far \nwestern New York should stay dry most of Sunday, although a few \nlight showers should arrive by late afternoon or evening.\n\nThe coastal low is then forecast to slowly meander northeast along \nthe New England coast Sunday night through Tuesday, weakening with \ntime. The greatest rain chances and greatest western extent of the \nrain shield will be Sunday night, with showers then gradually \ntapering off and ending from west to east late Sunday night\nthrough Monday as the low weakens and moves northeast.",
